S.1153, Khara. It states that Siddayadeva-Maharaja of the family of Mukkanti Kadu[vatti*] 
gave away the village of Aduru to the temple of Ganpati Prasanna-Kesavadeva at Motupalli 
for the merit of Kakatiya Ganapatideva.Read more (1 KB)

Tripurantakesvara, dated S. 11[8]3, (Durmati), (2nd year of Rudradeva-Maharaja). Damaged. 
States that a general of Rudradeva-Maharaja (the name of the general is missing) gave 50 cows 
for a perpetual lamp in the temple of Tripurantaka Deva.Read more (1 KB)
